# Story: someone who zooms about never has to wonder where they are. ⌃⌥M shows the whole arrangement in small with the
# space in view marked; it stays, and a click in it goes straight to a window. Someone with animation off has it show by itself
# after every move of the view, also when nobody asked for the move.
# Reference: A26 (docs/features/F26-minimap.md).
# As the first build shipped it: the whole map of shortcuts, of which nine ship now (22-nine-keys.sim).
set shortcuts all
# As the first build shipped it: the Desktop is a place on the map, between two windows, and can be clicked there.
set desktopColumn true
# The ring is an option (collab/QUESTIONS.md, Q29). Here it says where the keyboard is, and that the line is round that very window.
set focusRing true
open Safari
open Notes
open Mail
dock 101 left
dock 102 right
# As it ships, nothing appears by itself.
zoom 101
expect minimap none
show-all
set minimapDuration 0.9
# Docking from the widest view changes the arrangement, not the view.
expect minimap none
zoom 101
expect minimap 101
# It goes by itself.
wait 0.8
expect minimap 101
wait 0.2
expect minimap none
# A second move takes the first one's place, and the time starts again.
neighbor right
expect minimap desktop
wait 0.6
neighbor right
expect minimap 102
wait 0.6
expect minimap 102
wait 0.4
expect minimap none
# Everything is on screen then: a small picture of it would say nothing. One that is still up goes.
zoom 101
expect minimap 101
show-all
expect minimap none
# The move nobody asked for: the framed window closes, and the one below it fills the view.
open Xcode
dock 104 beside 102 bottom
zoom 102
wait 1
close 102
expect camera 104
expect minimap 104
wait 1
close 104
# On demand it stays five seconds and takes clicks.
open Terminal
dock 105 right
zoom 101
wait 1
minimap
expect minimap 101
wait 4.9
expect minimap 101
map 105
expect camera 105
expect fills 105
expect ring 105
expect minimap 105
# Its job done, it goes like any other.
wait 1
expect minimap none
# A passing one lets clicks through.
zoom 101
map 105
expect fail
expect camera 101
wait 1
# ⌃⌥M again puts it away, and so does a click beside the map.
minimap
minimap
expect minimap none
minimap
map beside
expect minimap none
expect camera 101
# The Desktop can be clicked too, and the window floating on it comes back into view.
expect hidden 103
minimap
map desktop
expect camera desktop
expect visible 103
# Held, ⌃⌥M is like a held ⌃⌥Space: hold to look, let go to land. The panel is at 600,690, 240 by 154, on this display.
wait 1
zoom 101
wait 1
keydown ctrl+opt+m
wait 8
expect minimap 101
cursor 800 780
wait 0.1
keyup ctrl+opt+m
expect camera 105
expect ring 105
expect minimap 105
wait 1
expect minimap none
# Let go with the pointer over nothing, it is only put away.
cursor 300 300
keydown ctrl+opt+m
wait 1
keyup ctrl+opt+m
expect minimap none
expect camera 105
# ⎋ while holding gives up. It is ⌃⌥⎋ then, which would pause Arbor: it does not.
keydown ctrl+opt+m
wait 1
key ctrl+opt+escape
expect minimap none
expect hidden 101
keyup ctrl+opt+m
expect camera 105
# Its time does not run out under the pointer.
key ctrl+opt+m
cursor 720 780
wait 30
expect minimap 105
cursor 300 300
wait 5.2
expect minimap none
# A tap stays.
key ctrl+opt+m
expect minimap 105
# A pause takes it down at once; resuming is not a move.
pause
expect minimap none
resume
expect minimap none
# With nothing docked there is nothing to map.
float-all
minimap
expect fail
